%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/OrderRequest.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Automatic rejection — <<<@Validated>>> + <<<@Valid>>>

  Placing <<<@Validated>>> on the service class and <<<@Valid>>> on the <<<@RequestBody>>> parameter
  is all that is required.  When a request fails validation, OfficeFloor returns <<<400 Bad Request>>>
  before the method body is entered — the service method is never called for an invalid request:

%{snippet|file=${basedir}/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/order.POST.yml|ignoreDownloadError=false}

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/PlaceOrderService.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  This is identical to how <<<@Validated>>> works on a Spring <<<@RestController>>> — OfficeFloor
  delegates to Spring's validation infrastructure without any additional configuration.



*Manual error handling — <<<BindingResult>>>

  When the service method needs to inspect validation errors itself — for example to return a
  structured error body — declare a <<<BindingResult>>> parameter immediately after the
  <<<@Valid>>>-annotated parameter.  OfficeFloor passes validation errors through <<<BindingResult>>>
  and the method body always executes, even when there are errors:

%{snippet|file=${basedir}/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/order/binding.POST.yml|ignoreDownloadError=false}

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/PlaceOrderBindingService.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  The <<<BindingResult>>> parameter must immediately follow the <<<@Valid>>>-annotated parameter,
  exactly as required in Spring MVC.



*Structured error response — <<<@RestControllerAdvice>>> for <<<MethodArgumentNotValidException>>>

  When the service method does not declare a <<<BindingResult>>> parameter, Spring throws
  <<<MethodArgumentNotValidException>>> on validation failure.  A <<<@RestControllerAdvice>>>
  catches this and returns a structured body — typically a map of field names to error messages —
  that clients can display field-by-field:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/ValidationErrorResponse.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/ValidationControllerAdvice.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  The advice works identically for OfficeFloor service methods and Spring <<<@RestController>>>
  methods — no additional configuration is needed.  The test verifies both the 400 status and
  the per-field error structure:

+--
// response body for { "product": "", "quantity": 0 }
{
  "errors": {
    "product":  ["Product name is required"],
    "quantity": ["Quantity must be at least 1"]
  }
}
+--



*Custom constraint validators

  Custom <<<@Constraint>>> annotations backed by a <<<ConstraintValidator>>> implementation work
  without any change.  They are invoked by the Jakarta Bean Validation machinery during
  <<<@Valid>>> processing — OfficeFloor does not intercept or replace that machinery.

  The example below validates that an order quantity is even (items sold in pairs).  The
  validator uses <<<disableDefaultConstraintViolation()>>> and <<<buildConstraintViolationWithTemplate()>>>
  to produce a specific message, exactly as in a plain Spring MVC application:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/EvenQuantity.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/EvenQuantityValidator.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  The annotation is applied to the request DTO alongside standard Jakarta constraints:

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/BulkOrderRequest.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}

  The service method and YAML are identical to the standard <<<@Valid>>> pattern — no special
  configuration is needed for custom constraints:

%{snippet|file=${basedir}/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/order/bulk.POST.yml|ignoreDownloadError=false}

%{snippet|id=tutorial|file=${basedir}/src/main/java/net/officefloor/tutorial/springrestvalidation/PlaceBulkOrderService.java|ignoreDownloadError=false}



*Validation in a multi-function pipeline

  <<<@Valid>>> runs before the body of the function that declares it.  In a single function this is automatic.  In
  a multi-function pipeline the position of the validating function decides when validation runs.

  Put the validating function first.  If a load function ran first, an invalid body against a missing id would
  return 404 before the body was checked.  With validation first, the invalid body returns 400.

  The {{{../SpringRestCrudHttpServer/index.html}REST CRUD Orchestration}} tutorial shows this ordering for
  create and update.



